 ## Lifecycle snapshot race correction
 
-The copied lifecycle helper no longer launches untracked daemon report-snapshot threads. Each capture gets a private stop event, non-daemon thread, retained authenticated report/generated-flow paths, and an exception/result channel. Every startup-interrupt, detached-ready, ready-interrupt, and force-teardown caller stops and joins its exact thread with a bounded timeout. After the stop request, the worker copies from the retained report path even when the session is gone or the runner has exited. The stop operation re-raises worker copy/ownership failures and requires the terminal report copy before phase cleanup or acceptance can continue. When a generated flow was observed, its retained copy is also mandatory.
+The copied lifecycle helper no longer launches untracked daemon report-snapshot threads. Each capture gets a private stop event, an authentication event, a non-daemon thread, retained authenticated report/generated-flow paths, and an exception/result channel. The worker signals authentication only after binding the live exact PID/device argv, retaining both paths, and recording ownership. Every startup-interrupt, detached-ready, ready-interrupt, and force-teardown caller waits boundedly for that authentication (and verifies the observed PID when available) before interrupting or finishing the runner. This handshake does not wait for runner readiness or flow completion, so the startup-interrupt case retains its `starting` timing semantics. Worker errors and authentication timeouts fail synchronously.
 
+Every caller then stops and joins its exact thread with a bounded timeout. After the stop request, the worker copies from the retained report path even when the session is gone or the runner has exited. The stop operation re-raises worker copy/ownership failures and requires the terminal report copy before phase cleanup or acceptance can continue. When a generated flow was observed, its retained copy is also mandatory.
+
 This does not weaken report evidence. `copy_report_snapshot` still tolerates only disappearing `.tmp` files from atomic writes; a missing retained report path, missing stable files, and all unrelated copy failures raise through the caller. Detached readiness still requires the retained report and passed status, and the helper cannot complete while a capture thread remains live.
 
